Package: searchengine
Version: 1.0.0
Section: web
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Your Name <your-email@example.com>
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31)
Recommends: libnspr4, libnss3, libatk1.0-0t64, libatk-bridge2.0-0t64, libcups2t64,
 libdrm2, libxkbcommon0, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxfixes3, libxrandr2,
 libgbm1, libasound2t64, libatspi2.0-0t64, libxshmfence1, libgtk-3-0t64,
 libcairo-gobject2, libcairo2, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0, libxcursor1, libxcb-shm0,
 libpangocairo-1.0-0
Suggests: docker.io
Description: Custom hybrid search engine (BM25 + semantic)
 Crawler, inverted index, BM25 ranking, and semantic search
 over SQLite/MySQL/PostgreSQL. Hexagonal architecture, in Go.
 .
 Recommends pulls in the shared libraries crawl-server's optional real-
 browser rendering (Renderer=chromium/firefox, see
 internal/adapters/browserfetcher) needs to launch either Playwright
 browser engine -- without them, a crawl configured to use one fails with
 a "launching <browser>: ... error while loading shared libraries"/missing-
 dependency error rather than crashing the process; every other feature
 (the default Renderer=none plain-HTTP fetch included) is unaffected
 either way. Recommends rather than Depends since rendering is opt-in, not
 every deployment needs it, and a minimal install (apt-get install
 --no-install-recommends) can still skip this GTK/Cairo stack entirely.
